                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is a serious dungeon crawler game. You play as a blobby little character with a sword (of farting or some other bodily function), a pair of pants, and a hat. The character appears differently based on the equipment that you pick up in the game, which is an interesting twist to the normal pixel-based dungeon crawlers. \n\nYou will hack your way through monsters and nests as you progress down the scrungeon. There will be occasional levels that are shops where you can often buy equipment that is worse than the RNG equipment that you find in the scrungeons.\n\nOne of the most interesting features that this game has to offer is the physics behind slain foes. If you kill off a bunch of baddies, they leave viscera around the floor, which will slow you down--the more chunks of bodies, the slower you move, which can often lead to death.\n\nWhen you die, you can continue where you left off, without the awesome equipment that helped get you there, which often means continued runs will not go nearly as well.\n\nThe downside -- the monsters are very repetitive, with only a few models that you will encounter.\nThe upside(s) -- The developer is very active, and has already released a pretty big update to the game. It is also one of the most entertaining way to spend 15 minutes and get absolutely pissed off that you died when things were going so well.",
